<ul style="list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(300px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 16px"><li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; border-radius: var(--radius-card)"><span style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">01</span><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink)">Agents never talk to each other</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-muted)">They only pass immutable artifacts, and each one links back to the issue it came from.</p></li><li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; border-radius: var(--radius-card)"><span style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">02</span><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink)">Smallest context first</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-muted)">Five retrieval layers. The coding agent may only read the files listed in its context manifest.</p></li><li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; border-radius: var(--radius-card)"><span style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">03</span><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink)">Graphs come from code</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-muted)">Dependency and impact graphs come from static analysis, never from the model.</p></li><li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; border-radius: var(--radius-card)"><span style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">04</span><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink)">Budgets stop the work</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-muted)">Start on the cheapest capable model; going over budget pauses the run for my approval.</p></li><li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; border-radius: var(--radius-card)"><span style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">05</span><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink)">Default deny</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-muted)">Each agent gets only the permissions its role needs, and I can pause or override any stage.</p></li><li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; border-radius: var(--radius-card)"><span style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">06</span><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink)">Knowledge lives with the code</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-muted)">The nearest CLAUDE.md wins. Humans write the guidance; agents read it before code.</p></li></ul>
